meta {
  name: Get My Subscription
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/subscription
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

docs {
  # Get My Subscription

  The master's own subscription: the one currently granting access, the access
  deadline, and the full purchase history.

  Runs under `ensure.master:allow-expired` — unlike every other master endpoint
  it stays reachable **after** the subscription runs out, so the app can render
  "expired on …, renew" instead of a bare 403. Blocked masters (`is_active =
  false`) and applications still under review are still rejected.

  **Response 200:**
  ```json
  {
    "data": {
      "current": {
        "id": 12,
        "plan_name": "1 месяц",
        "price_paid": 150.00,
        "duration_days": 30,
        "status": "active",
        "status_label": "Активна",
        "starts_at": "2026-08-01",
        "expires_at": "2026-08-31",
        "days_left": 17
      },
      "access_expires_at": "2026-08-31",
      "has_active_access": true,
      "pending_request": null,
      "history": []
    }
  }
  ```

  | Field               | Type          | Description                                                    |
  |---------------------|---------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
  | `current`           | object\|null  | Running subscription, or the next queued one; `null` when access is closed |
  | `access_expires_at` | date\|null    | Derived from subscriptions                                      |
  | `pending_request`   | object\|null  | Plan request awaiting the administrator — same shape as in `subscription-requests` |
  | `status`            | string        | `pending` / `active` / `expired` / `cancelled`                  |
  | `days_left`         | int           | 0 once the end date has passed                                  |

  **Errors:**
  - `401` — no token
  - `403` — no master profile on this account, or it is blocked (see `reason`)
}
